#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "A free IBM course on quantum information and computation"
msgstr "Un curs IBM gratuit despre informație și calcul cuantic"

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Bloch sphere"
msgstr "Sfera Bloch"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"There's a useful geometric way to represent qubit states known as the *Bloch sphere*.\n"
"It's very convenient, but unfortunately it only works for qubits — the analogous representation no longer corresponds to a spherical object once we have three or more classical states of our system.\n"
msgstr ""
"Există o modalitate geometrică utilă de a reprezenta stările unui qubit, cunoscută drept *sfera Bloch*.\n"
"Este foarte convenabilă, dar din păcate funcționează doar pentru qubiți — reprezentarea analogă nu mai corespunde unui obiect sferic odată ce sistemul nostru are trei sau mai multe stări clasice.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Qubit states as points on a sphere {#qubit-states-as-points-on-a-sphere}"
msgstr "Stările qubitului ca puncte pe o sferă {#qubit-states-as-points-on-a-sphere}"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Let's start by thinking about a quantum state vector of a qubit: $\\alpha \\vert 0\\rangle + \\beta \\vert 1\\rangle$.\n"
"We can restrict our attention to vectors for which $\\alpha$ is a nonnegative real number because every qubit state vector is equivalent up to a global phase to one for which $\\alpha \\geq 0$.\n"
"This allows us to write\n"
msgstr ""
"Să începem prin a gândi un vector de stare cuantică al unui qubit: $\\alpha \\vert 0\\rangle + \\beta \\vert 1\\rangle.$\n"
"Ne putem restrânge atenția la vectorii pentru care $\\alpha$ este un număr real nenegativ, deoarece orice vector de stare al unui qubit este echivalent, la o fază globală, cu unul pentru care $\\alpha \\geq 0.$\n"
"Aceasta ne permite să scriem\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\psi\\rangle = \\cos\\bigl(\\theta/2\\bigr) \\vert 0\\rangle + e^{i\\phi} \\sin\\bigl(\\theta/2\\bigr) \\vert 1\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\psi\\rangle = \\cos\\bigl(\\theta/2\\bigr) \\vert 0\\rangle + e^{i\\phi} \\sin\\bigl(\\theta/2\\bigr) \\vert 1\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"for two real numbers $\\theta \\in [0,\\pi]$ and $\\phi\\in[0,2\\pi)$.\n"
"Here, we're allowing $\\theta$ to range from $0$ to $\\pi$ and dividing by $2$ in the argument of sine and cosine because this is a conventional way to parameterize vectors of this sort, and it will make things simpler a bit later on.\n"
msgstr ""
"pentru două numere reale $\\theta \\in [0,\\pi]$ și $\\phi\\in[0,2\\pi)$.\n"
"Aici, îl lăsăm pe $\\theta$ să varieze de la $0$ la $\\pi$ și împărțim la $2$ în argumentul sinusului și cosinusului deoarece aceasta este o modalitate convențională de a parametriza vectori de acest fel și va simplifica lucrurile puțin mai târziu.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now, it isn't quite the case that the numbers $\\theta$ and $\\phi$ are uniquely determined by a given quantum state vector $\\alpha \\vert 0\\rangle + \\beta \\vert 1\\rangle$, but it is nearly so.\n"
"In particular, if $\\beta = 0$, then $\\theta = 0$ and it doesn't make any difference what value $\\phi$ takes, so it can be chosen arbitrarily.\n"
"Similarly, if $\\alpha = 0$, then $\\theta = \\pi$, and once again $\\phi$ is irrelevant (as our state is equivalent to $e^{i\\phi}\\vert 1\\rangle$ for any $\\phi$ up to a global phase).\n"
"If, however, neither $\\alpha$ nor $\\beta$ is zero, then there's a unique choice for the pair $(\\theta,\\phi)$ for which $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ is equivalent to $\\alpha\\vert 0\\rangle + \\beta\\vert 1\\rangle$ up to a global phase.\n"
msgstr ""
"Acum, nu este chiar adevărat că numerele $\\theta$ și $\\phi$ sunt determinate în mod unic de un vector de stare cuantică dat $\\alpha \\vert 0\\rangle + \\beta \\vert 1\\rangle$, dar aproape că așa stau lucrurile.\n"
"În particular, dacă $\\beta = 0$, atunci $\\theta = 0$ și nu contează ce valoare ia $\\phi$, deci poate fi ales arbitrar.\n"
"Similar, dacă $\\alpha = 0$, atunci $\\theta = \\pi$, și din nou $\\phi$ este irelevant (deoarece starea noastră este echivalentă cu $e^{i\\phi}\\vert 1\\rangle$ pentru orice $\\phi$ la o fază globală).\n"
"Dacă însă nici $\\alpha$ și nici $\\beta$ nu este zero, atunci există o alegere unică pentru perechea $(\\theta,\\phi)$ pentru care $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ este echivalent cu $\\alpha\\vert 0\\rangle + \\beta\\vert 1\\rangle$ la o fază globală.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next, let's consider the density matrix representation of this state.\n"
msgstr "Să considerăm acum reprezentarea prin matrice de densitate a acestei stări.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\cos^2(\\theta/2) & e^{-i\\phi}\\cos(\\theta/2)\\sin(\\theta/2)\\\\[2mm]\n"
"e^{i\\phi}\\cos(\\theta/2)\\sin(\\theta/2) & \\sin^2(\\theta/2)\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\cos^2(\\theta/2) & e^{-i\\phi}\\cos(\\theta/2)\\sin(\\theta/2)\\\\[2mm]\n"
"e^{i\\phi}\\cos(\\theta/2)\\sin(\\theta/2) & \\sin^2(\\theta/2)\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We can use some trigonometric identities,\n"
msgstr "Putem folosi câteva identități trigonometrice,\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{gathered}\n"
"\\cos^2(\\theta/2) = \\frac{1 + \\cos(\\theta)}{2},\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\sin^2(\\theta/2) = \\frac{1 - \\cos(\\theta)}{2},\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\cos(\\theta/2) \\sin(\\theta/2) = \\frac{\\sin(\\theta)}{2},\n"
"\\end{gathered}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{gathered}\n"
"\\cos^2(\\theta/2) = \\frac{1 + \\cos(\\theta)}{2},\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\sin^2(\\theta/2) = \\frac{1 - \\cos(\\theta)}{2},\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\cos(\\theta/2) \\sin(\\theta/2) = \\frac{\\sin(\\theta)}{2},\n"
"\\end{gathered}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "as well as the formula $e^{i\\phi} = \\cos(\\phi) + i\\sin(\\phi)$, to simplify the density matrix as follows.\n"
msgstr "precum și formula $e^{i\\phi} = \\cos(\\phi) + i\\sin(\\phi)$, pentru a simplifica matricea de densitate după cum urmează.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert\n"
"= \\frac{1}{2}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 + \\cos(\\theta) & (\\cos(\\phi) - i \\sin(\\phi)) \\sin(\\theta)\\\\[1mm]\n"
"(\\cos(\\phi) + i \\sin(\\phi)) \\sin(\\theta) & 1 - \\cos(\\theta)\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert\n"
"= \\frac{1}{2}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 + \\cos(\\theta) & (\\cos(\\phi) - i \\sin(\\phi)) \\sin(\\theta)\\\\[1mm]\n"
"(\\cos(\\phi) + i \\sin(\\phi)) \\sin(\\theta) & 1 - \\cos(\\theta)\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This makes it easy to express this density matrix as a linear combination of the Pauli matrices:\n"
msgstr "Aceasta face ușoară exprimarea acestei matrice de densitate ca o combinație liniară a matricelor Pauli:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"  \\mathbb{I} =\n"
"  \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"    1 & 0\\\\[1mm]\n"
"    0 & 1\n"
"  \\end{pmatrix},\n"
"  \\quad\n"
"  \\sigma_x =\n"
"  \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"    0 & 1\\\\[1mm]\n"
"    1 & 0\n"
"  \\end{pmatrix},\n"
"  \\quad\n"
"  \\sigma_y =\n"
"  \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"    0 & -i\\\\[1mm]\n"
"    i & 0\n"
"  \\end{pmatrix},\n"
"  \\quad\n"
"  \\sigma_z =\n"
"  \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"    1 & 0\\\\[1mm]\n"
"    0 & -1\n"
"  \\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"  \\mathbb{I} =\n"
"  \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"    1 & 0\\\\[1mm]\n"
"    0 & 1\n"
"  \\end{pmatrix},\n"
"  \\quad\n"
"  \\sigma_x =\n"
"  \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"    0 & 1\\\\[1mm]\n"
"    1 & 0\n"
"  \\end{pmatrix},\n"
"  \\quad\n"
"  \\sigma_y =\n"
"  \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"    0 & -i\\\\[1mm]\n"
"    i & 0\n"
"  \\end{pmatrix},\n"
"  \\quad\n"
"  \\sigma_z =\n"
"  \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"    1 & 0\\\\[1mm]\n"
"    0 & -1\n"
"  \\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Specifically, we conclude that\n"
msgstr "Mai precis, concluzionăm că\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert\n"
"= \\frac{\\mathbb{I} + \\sin(\\theta) \\cos(\\phi)\\sigma_x + \\sin(\\theta)\\sin(\\phi) \\sigma_y + \\cos(\\theta) \\sigma_z}{2}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert\n"
"= \\frac{\\mathbb{I} + \\sin(\\theta) \\cos(\\phi)\\sigma_x + \\sin(\\theta)\\sin(\\phi) \\sigma_y + \\cos(\\theta) \\sigma_z}{2}.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The coefficients of $\\sigma_x$, $\\sigma_y$, and $\\sigma_z$ in the numerator of this expression are all real numbers, so we can collect them together to form a vector in an ordinary, three-dimensional Euclidean space.\n"
msgstr "Coeficienții lui $\\sigma_x,$ $\\sigma_y,$ și $\\sigma_z$ din numărătorul acestei expresii sunt cu toții numere reale, deci îi putem aduna pentru a forma un vector într-un spațiu euclidian obișnuit, tridimensional.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\bigl(\\sin(\\theta) \\cos(\\phi), \\sin(\\theta)\\sin(\\phi), \\cos(\\theta)\\bigr)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\bigl(\\sin(\\theta) \\cos(\\phi), \\sin(\\theta)\\sin(\\phi), \\cos(\\theta)\\bigr)\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In fact, this is a unit vector.\n"
"Using *spherical coordinates* it can be written as $(1,\\theta,\\phi)$.\n"
"The first coordinate, $1$, represents the *radius* or *radial distance* (which is always $1$ in this case), $\\theta$ represents the *polar angle*, and $\\phi$ represents the *azimuthal angle*.\n"
msgstr ""
"De fapt, acesta este un vector unitar.\n"
"Folosind *coordonate sferice* poate fi scris ca $(1,\\theta,\\phi).$\n"
"Prima coordonată, $1,$ reprezintă *raza* sau *distanța radială* (care este întotdeauna $1$ în acest caz), $\\theta$ reprezintă *unghiul polar*, iar $\\phi$ reprezintă *unghiul azimutal*.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In words, thinking about a sphere as the planet Earth, the polar angle $\\theta$ is how far we rotate south from the north pole to reach the point being described, from $0$ to $\\pi = 180^{\\circ}$, while the azimuthal angle $\\phi$ is how far we rotate east from the prime meridian, from $0$ to $2\\pi = 360^{\\circ}$.\n"
"This assumes that we define the prime meridian to be the curve on the surface of the sphere from one pole to the other that passes through the positive $x$-axis.\n"
msgstr ""
"Cu alte cuvinte, gândind o sferă ca planeta Pământ, unghiul polar $\\theta$ reprezintă cât de mult rotim spre sud față de polul nord pentru a ajunge la punctul descris, de la $0$ la $\\pi = 180^{\\circ}$, în timp ce unghiul azimutal $\\phi$ reprezintă cât de mult rotim spre est față de meridianul principal, de la $0$ la $2\\pi = 360^{\\circ}$.\n"
"Presupunem că definim meridianul principal ca fiind curba de pe suprafața sferei de la un pol la celălalt care trece prin axa $x$ pozitivă.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Illustration of a point on the unit 2-sphere in terms of its spherical coordinates.](/learning/images/courses/general-formulation-of-quantum-information/density-matrices/spherical-coordinates.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Illustration of a point on the unit 2-sphere in terms of its spherical coordinates.](/learning/images/courses/general-formulation-of-quantum-information/density-matrices/spherical-coordinates.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Every point on the sphere can be described in this way — which is to say that the points we obtain when we range over all possible pure states of a qubit correspond precisely to a sphere in $3$ real dimensions.\n"
"(This sphere is typically called the *unit $2$-sphere* because the surface of this sphere is two-dimensional.)\n"
msgstr ""
"Fiecare punct de pe sferă poate fi descris în acest mod — adică punctele obținute când parcurgem toate stările pure posibile ale unui qubit corespund exact unei sfere în $3$ dimensiuni reale.\n"
"(Această sferă este numită de obicei *$2$-sfera unitară* deoarece suprafața acestei sfere este bidimensională.)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "When we associate points on the unit $2$-sphere with pure states of qubits, we obtain the *Bloch sphere* representation these states.\n"
msgstr "Când asociem punctele de pe $2$-sfera unitară cu stările pure ale qubiților, obținem reprezentarea prin *sfera Bloch* a acestor stări.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Six important examples {#six-important-examples}"
msgstr "Șase exemple importante {#six-important-examples}"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*The standard basis* $\\{\\vert 0\\rangle,\\vert 1\\rangle\\}$.\n"
"Let's start with the state $\\vert 0\\rangle$.\n"
"As a density matrix it can be written like this.\n"
msgstr ""
"*Baza standard* $\\{\\vert 0\\rangle,\\vert 1\\rangle\\}$.\n"
"Să începem cu starea $\\vert 0\\rangle$.\n"
"Ca matrice de densitate, poate fi scrisă astfel.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\vert 0 \\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert = \\frac{\\mathbb{I} + \\sigma_z}{2}\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\vert 0 \\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert = \\frac{\\mathbb{I} + \\sigma_z}{2}\n"
"   $$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   By collecting the coefficients of the Pauli matrices in the numerator, we see that the corresponding point on the unit $2$-sphere using Cartesian coordinates is $(0,0,1)$.\n"
"   In spherical coordinates this point is $(1,0,\\phi)$, where $\\phi$ can be any angle.\n"
"   This is consistent with the expression\n"
msgstr ""
"   Adunând coeficienții matricelor Pauli din numărător, observăm că punctul corespunzător pe $2$-sfera unitară în coordonate carteziene este $(0,0,1)$.\n"
"   În coordonate sferice, acest punct este $(1,0,\\phi)$, unde $\\phi$ poate fi orice unghi.\n"
"   Aceasta este consistent cu expresia\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\vert 0\\rangle = \\cos(0) \\vert 0\\rangle + e^{i \\phi} \\sin(0) \\vert 1\\rangle,\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\vert 0\\rangle = \\cos(0) \\vert 0\\rangle + e^{i \\phi} \\sin(0) \\vert 1\\rangle,\n"
"   $$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   which also works for any $\\phi$.\n"
"   Intuitively speaking, the polar angle $\\theta$ is zero, so we're at the north pole of the Bloch sphere, where the azimuthal angle is irrelevant.\n"
msgstr ""
"   care funcționează și ea pentru orice $\\phi$.\n"
"   Intuitiv, unghiul polar $\\theta$ este zero, deci ne aflăm la polul nord al sferei Bloch, unde unghiul azimutal este irelevant.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "   Along similar lines, the density matrix for the state $\\vert 1\\rangle$ can be written like so.\n"
msgstr "   În mod similar, matricea de densitate pentru starea $\\vert 1\\rangle$ poate fi scrisă astfel.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\vert 1 \\rangle \\langle 1 \\vert = \\frac{\\mathbb{I} - \\sigma_z}{2}\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\vert 1 \\rangle \\langle 1 \\vert = \\frac{\\mathbb{I} - \\sigma_z}{2}\n"
"   $$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "   This time the Cartesian coordinates are $(0,0,-1)$. In spherical coordinates this point is $(1,\\pi,\\phi)$ where $\\phi$ can be any angle. In this case the polar angle is all the way to $\\pi$, so we're at the south pole where the azimuthal angle is again irrelevant.\n"
msgstr "   De data aceasta coordonatele carteziene sunt $(0,0,-1)$. În coordonate sferice, acest punct este $(1,\\pi,\\phi)$ unde $\\phi$ poate fi orice unghi. În acest caz unghiul polar ajunge la $\\pi$, deci ne aflăm la polul sud, unde unghiul azimutal este din nou irelevant.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*The basis $\\{\\vert + \\rangle, \\vert - \\rangle\\}$.*\n"
"We have these expressions for the density matrices corresponding to these states.\n"
msgstr ""
"*Baza $\\{\\vert + \\rangle, \\vert - \\rangle\\}$.*\n"
"Avem aceste expresii pentru matricele de densitate corespunzătoare acestor stări.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\begin{aligned}\n"
"   \\vert {+} \\rangle\\langle {+} \\vert & = \\frac{\\mathbb{I} + \\sigma_x}{2}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\vert {-} \\rangle\\langle {-} \\vert & = \\frac{\\mathbb{I} - \\sigma_x}{2}\n"
"   \\end{aligned}\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\begin{aligned}\n"
"   \\vert {+} \\rangle\\langle {+} \\vert & = \\frac{\\mathbb{I} + \\sigma_x}{2}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\vert {-} \\rangle\\langle {-} \\vert & = \\frac{\\mathbb{I} - \\sigma_x}{2}\n"
"   \\end{aligned}\n"
"   $$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   The corresponding points on the unit $2$-sphere have Cartesian coordinates $(1,0,0)$ and $(-1,0,0)$,\n"
"   and spherical coordinates $(1,\\pi/2,0)$ and $(1,\\pi/2,\\pi)$, respectively.\n"
msgstr ""
"   Punctele corespunzătoare de pe $2$-sfera unitară au coordonate carteziene $(1,0,0)$ și $(-1,0,0)$,\n"
"   și coordonate sferice $(1,\\pi/2,0)$ și $(1,\\pi/2,\\pi)$, respectiv.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "   In words, $\\vert +\\rangle$ corresponds to the point where the positive $x$-axis intersects the unit $2$-sphere and $\\vert -\\rangle$ corresponds to the point where the negative $x$-axis intersects it. More intuitively, $\\vert +\\rangle$ is on the equator of the Bloch sphere where it meets the prime meridian, and $\\vert - \\rangle$ is on the equator on the opposite side of the sphere.\n"
msgstr "   Cu alte cuvinte, $\\vert +\\rangle$ corespunde punctului în care axa $x$ pozitivă intersectează $2$-sfera unitară, iar $\\vert -\\rangle$ corespunde punctului în care axa $x$ negativă o intersectează. Mai intuitiv, $\\vert +\\rangle$ se află pe ecuatorul sferei Bloch acolo unde aceasta întâlnește meridianul principal, iar $\\vert - \\rangle$ se află pe ecuator pe partea opusă a sferei.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*The basis* $\\{\\vert {+i} \\rangle, \\vert {-i} \\rangle\\}$.\n"
"As we saw earlier in the lesson, these two states are defined like this:\n"
msgstr ""
"*Baza* $\\{\\vert {+i} \\rangle, \\vert {-i} \\rangle\\}$.\n"
"Cum am văzut mai devreme în lecție, aceste două stări sunt definite astfel:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\begin{aligned}\n"
"   \\vert {+i} \\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 0 \\rangle + \\frac{i}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 1 \\rangle\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\vert {-i} \\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 0 \\rangle - \\frac{i}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 1 \\rangle.\n"
"   \\end{aligned}\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\begin{aligned}\n"
"   \\vert {+i} \\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 0 \\rangle + \\frac{i}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 1 \\rangle\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\vert {-i} \\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 0 \\rangle - \\frac{i}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 1 \\rangle.\n"
"   \\end{aligned}\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "   This time we have these expressions.\n"
msgstr "   De data aceasta avem aceste expresii.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\begin{aligned}\n"
"   \\vert {+i} \\rangle\\langle {+i} \\vert & = \\frac{\\mathbb{I} + \\sigma_y}{2}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\vert {-i} \\rangle\\langle {-i} \\vert & = \\frac{\\mathbb{I} - \\sigma_y}{2}\n"
"   \\end{aligned}\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\begin{aligned}\n"
"   \\vert {+i} \\rangle\\langle {+i} \\vert & = \\frac{\\mathbb{I} + \\sigma_y}{2}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\vert {-i} \\rangle\\langle {-i} \\vert & = \\frac{\\mathbb{I} - \\sigma_y}{2}\n"
"   \\end{aligned}\n"
"   $$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   The corresponding points on the unit $2$-sphere have Cartesian coordinates $(0,1,0)$ and $(0,-1,0)$,\n"
"   and spherical coordinates $(1,\\pi/2,\\pi/2)$ and $(1,\\pi/2,3\\pi/2)$, respectively.\n"
msgstr ""
"   Punctele corespunzătoare de pe $2$-sfera unitară au coordonate carteziene $(0,1,0)$ și $(0,-1,0)$,\n"
"   și coordonate sferice $(1,\\pi/2,\\pi/2)$ și $(1,\\pi/2,3\\pi/2)$, respectiv.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "   In words, $\\vert {+i} \\rangle$ corresponds to the point where the positive $y$-axis intersects the unit $2$-sphere and $\\vert {-i} \\rangle$ to the point where the negative $y$-axis intersects it.\n"
msgstr "   Cu alte cuvinte, $\\vert {+i} \\rangle$ corespunde punctului în care axa $y$ pozitivă intersectează $2$-sfera unitară, iar $\\vert {-i} \\rangle$ corespunde punctului în care axa $y$ negativă o intersectează.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Illustration of six examples of pure states on the Bloch sphere](/learning/images/courses/general-formulation-of-quantum-information/density-matrices/six-Bloch-sphere-points.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Illustration of six examples of pure states on the Bloch sphere](/learning/images/courses/general-formulation-of-quantum-information/density-matrices/six-Bloch-sphere-points.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here's another class of quantum state vectors that has appeared from time to time throughout this series, including previously in this lesson.\n"
msgstr "Iată o altă clasă de vectori de stare cuantică ce a apărut din când în când pe parcursul acestei serii, inclusiv anterior în această lecție.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi_{\\alpha} \\rangle = \\cos(\\alpha) \\vert 0\\rangle + \\sin(\\alpha) \\vert 1\\rangle \\qquad \\text{(for $\\alpha \\in [0,\\pi)$)}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi_{\\alpha} \\rangle = \\cos(\\alpha) \\vert 0\\rangle + \\sin(\\alpha) \\vert 1\\rangle \\qquad \\text{(for $\\alpha \\in [0,\\pi)$)}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The density matrix representation of each of these states is as follows.\n"
msgstr "Reprezentarea prin matrice de densitate a fiecăreia dintre aceste stări este următoarea.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi_{\\alpha} \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\alpha} \\vert =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\cos^2(\\alpha) & \\cos(\\alpha)\\sin(\\alpha)\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\cos(\\alpha)\\sin(\\alpha) & \\sin^2(\\alpha)\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\frac{\\mathbb{I} + \\sin(2\\alpha) \\sigma_x + \\cos(2\\alpha) \\sigma_z}{2}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi_{\\alpha} \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\alpha} \\vert =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\cos^2(\\alpha) & \\cos(\\alpha)\\sin(\\alpha)\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\cos(\\alpha)\\sin(\\alpha) & \\sin^2(\\alpha)\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\frac{\\mathbb{I} + \\sin(2\\alpha) \\sigma_x + \\cos(2\\alpha) \\sigma_z}{2}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The following figure illustrates the corresponding points on the Bloch sphere for a few choices for $\\alpha$.\n"
msgstr "Figura de mai jos ilustrează punctele corespunzătoare de pe sfera Bloch pentru câteva alegeri ale lui $\\alpha$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Illustration of real-valued qubit state vectors on the Bloch sphere](/learning/images/courses/general-formulation-of-quantum-information/density-matrices/real-Bloch-sphere-points.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Illustration of real-valued qubit state vectors on the Bloch sphere](/learning/images/courses/general-formulation-of-quantum-information/density-matrices/real-Bloch-sphere-points.avif)\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Convex combinations of points {#convex-combinations-of-points}"
msgstr "Combinații convexe de puncte {#convex-combinations-of-points}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Similar to what we have already discussed for density matrices, we can take convex combinations of points on the Bloch sphere to obtain representations of qubit density matrices.\n"
"In general, this results in points *inside* of the Bloch sphere, which represent density matrices of states that are not pure.\n"
"Sometimes we refer to the *Bloch ball* when we wish to be explicit about the inclusion of points inside of the Bloch sphere as representations of qubit density matrices.\n"
msgstr ""
"Similar cu ceea ce am discutat deja pentru matricele de densitate, putem lua combinații convexe ale punctelor de pe sfera Bloch pentru a obține reprezentări ale matricelor de densitate ale qubitului.\n"
"În general, aceasta duce la puncte *în interiorul* sferei Bloch, care reprezintă matricele de densitate ale stărilor care nu sunt pure.\n"
"Uneori ne referim la *bila Bloch* atunci când dorim să fim expliciți cu privire la includerea punctelor din interiorul sferei Bloch ca reprezentări ale matricelor de densitate ale qubitului.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For example, we've seen that the density matrix $\\frac{1}{2}\\mathbb{I}$, which represents the completely mixed state of a qubit, can be written in these two alternative ways:\n"
msgstr "De exemplu, am văzut că matricea de densitate $\\frac{1}{2}\\mathbb{I}$, care reprezintă starea complet mixtă a unui qubit, poate fi scrisă în aceste două moduri alternative:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\mathbb{I} = \\frac{1}{2} \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert + \\frac{1}{2} \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle 1\\vert\n"
"\\quad\\text{and}\\quad\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\mathbb{I} = \\frac{1}{2} \\vert +\\rangle\\langle +\\vert + \\frac{1}{2} \\vert -\\rangle\\langle -\\vert.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\mathbb{I} = \\frac{1}{2} \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert + \\frac{1}{2} \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle 1\\vert\n"
"\\quad\\text{and}\\quad\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\mathbb{I} = \\frac{1}{2} \\vert +\\rangle\\langle +\\vert + \\frac{1}{2} \\vert -\\rangle\\langle -\\vert.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We also have\n"
msgstr "Avem de asemenea\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\mathbb{I} =\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\vert {+i}\\rangle\\langle {+i} \\vert\n"
"+ \\frac{1}{2} \\vert {-i} \\rangle\\langle {-i}\\vert,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\mathbb{I} =\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\vert {+i}\\rangle\\langle {+i} \\vert\n"
"+ \\frac{1}{2} \\vert {-i} \\rangle\\langle {-i}\\vert,\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"and more generally we can use any two orthogonal qubit state vectors (which will always correspond to two antipodal points on the Bloch sphere).\n"
"If we average the corresponding points on the Bloch sphere in a similar way, we obtain the same point, which in this case is at the center of the sphere.\n"
"This is consistent with the observation that\n"
msgstr ""
"și mai general putem folosi orice doi vectori de stare ortogonali ai qubitului (care vor corespunde întotdeauna la două puncte antipodale pe sfera Bloch).\n"
"Dacă facem media punctelor corespunzătoare de pe sfera Bloch într-un mod similar, obținem același punct, care în acest caz se află în centrul sferei.\n"
"Aceasta este consistent cu observația că\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\mathbb{I} = \\frac{\\mathbb{I} + 0 \\cdot \\sigma_x + 0 \\cdot \\sigma_y + 0 \\cdot \\sigma_z}{2},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\mathbb{I} = \\frac{\\mathbb{I} + 0 \\cdot \\sigma_x + 0 \\cdot \\sigma_y + 0 \\cdot \\sigma_z}{2},\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "giving us the Cartesian coordinates $(0,0,0)$.\n"
msgstr "ceea ce ne dă coordonatele carteziene $(0,0,0)$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A different example concerning convex combinations of Bloch sphere points is the one discussed in the previous subsection.\n"
msgstr "Un alt exemplu privind combinațiile convexe ale punctelor de pe sfera Bloch este cel discutat în subsecțiunea anterioară.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0 \\vert + \\frac{1}{2} \\vert +\\rangle\\langle + \\vert\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix} \\frac{3}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\cos^2(\\pi/8) \\vert \\psi_{\\pi/8} \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\pi/8}\\vert +\n"
"\\sin^2(\\pi/8) \\vert \\psi_{5\\pi/8} \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\vert\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0 \\vert + \\frac{1}{2} \\vert +\\rangle\\langle + \\vert\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix} \\frac{3}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\cos^2(\\pi/8) \\vert \\psi_{\\pi/8} \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\pi/8}\\vert +\n"
"\\sin^2(\\pi/8) \\vert \\psi_{5\\pi/8} \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\vert\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The following figure illustrates these two different ways of obtaining this density matrix as a convex combination of pure states.\n"
msgstr "Figura de mai jos ilustrează aceste două modalități diferite de a obține această matrice de densitate ca o combinație convexă de stări pure.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Illustration of the average of the zero state and the plus state on the Bloch sphere](/learning/images/courses/general-formulation-of-quantum-information/density-matrices/Bloch-sphere-zero-plus-average.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Illustration of the average of the zero state and the plus state on the Bloch sphere](/learning/images/courses/general-formulation-of-quantum-information/density-matrices/Bloch-sphere-zero-plus-average.avif)\n"
